Important Keywords/methods:
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
page.goto("<url>")                                      → Navigates to the given website URL.
page.url                                                → Returns the current URL of the webpage.
page.title()                                            → Returns the title of the page.
page.wait_for_timeout(<milliseconds>)                   → Waits for the given time (in milliseconds).
time.sleep(<seconds>)                                   → Python’s built-in sleep. Takes seconds.
page.get_by_text(re.compile(".*Welcome.*"))             → Locates element using Regular Expressions.
.fill("<value>")                                        → Enters the given value into an input field/textbox.
.locator("<locator>")                                   → Finds elements on the webpage. Accepts **CSS and XPath**.
.count()                                                → Returns how many elements match a locator.
.text_content()                                         → Returns the text inside the element.
.first.text_content()                                   → Returns the text of the **first** matching element.
.last.text_content()                                    → Returns the text of the **last** matching element.
.nth(3).text_content()                                  → Returns the text of the element at index 3. (index starts from 0)
.all_text_contents()                                    → Returns a list of text from all matching elements.
.click()                                                → Clicks the element.
.get_attribute("<attribute>")                           → Returns the value of the given attribute.
.input_value()                                          → Returns the current value of an input field.
.check()                                                → Selects/checks a checkbox or radio button. (Ignores if already checked)
.uncheck()                                              → Unchecks a checkbox.
.is_checked()                                           → Returns True if checkbox/radio is checked, else False.

.select_option("India")                                 → Selects dropdown option(s) by label.
.select_option(label="India")
.select_option(label=["Red", "Blue", "Green"])

.select_option("germany")                               → Selects dropdown option(s) by value.
.select_option(value="germany")
.select_option(value=["Red", "White", "Green"])

.select_option(index=4)                                 → Selects dropdown option(s) by index.
.select_option(index=[2, 4])

Differences:
-------------------
inner_text() vs text_content():
    inner_text()      → Returns the visible and cleaned text users can see.
    text_content()    → Returns the raw text including whitespace, hidden text, and special chars.

all_inner_texts() vs all_text_contents()
    all_inner_texts()      → List of visible, cleaned text.
    all_text_contents()    → List of raw, uncleaned text.

all()
    → Returns list of ElementHandles (not text)
    Ex:
    elements = page.locator("div").all()
    for el in elements:
        print(el.text_content())

Assertions:
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
to_have_url()                           → URL matches expected value
to_have_title()                         → Title matches expected value
to_have_text()                          → Element text matches expected value
to_have_count()                         → Number of matched elements matches
to_have_attribute()                     → Attribute value matches

to_be_visible()                         → Element is visible
to_be_enabled()                         → Element is enabled

expect(locator).to_be_checked()         → Should be checked
expect(locator).not.to_be_checked()     → Should NOT be checked

Playwright Inbuilt Locators:
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
page.get_by_role()          to locate by explicit and implicit accessibility attributes.
                            Gdrive link: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ehh4vfWVdzLAQR8fka-wL31QDVlQWdu6/view?usp=drive_link
page.get_by_text()          to locate by text content.
page.get_by_label()         to locate a form control by associated label's text.
page.get_by_placeholder()   to locate an input by placeholder.
page.get_by_alt_text()      to locate an element, usually image, by its text alternative.
page.get_by_title()         to locate an element by its title attribute.
page.get_by_test_id()       to locate an element based on its data-testid attribute (other attributes can be configured).